    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406-a1">

                <pb facs="0727" n="657" xml:id="pg657"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in in No.
                    638.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Romero Rubio to
                        Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">June</hi> 2,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Friend</hi>: We can do nothing in this
                    capital in the affair of the Adriana, because, according to Mexican legislation,
                    it is necessary in the second instance to bring the affair before the circuit
                    court. The circuit court before whom this affair should be brought is now at
                    Culiacan. It is therefore at that place where the appeal should be taken, both
                    in the civil and criminal proceeding, in the event that an appeal is taken.</p>
                <p>Should this be the case, I have friends in Culiacan whom I can especially
                    recommend if you think it necessary.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. ROMERO RUBIO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
